# MCPZoo Development Rules

## ⚠️ CRITICAL: Never Test by Running Backend/Frontend
- DO NOT run backend servers (uvicorn, fastapi, etc.) to test code changes
- DO NOT run frontend dev servers (npm run dev, vite, etc.) to test functionality
- DO NOT start any development servers for testing purposes
- Only run servers if explicitly requested by the user

---

## MCPZoo Tasks CLI Commands Explanation

This Markdown document explains the commands implemented in the `tasks` CLI tool (Python script), aligned with the .clinerules file structure: `./tasks ENV NAMESPACE COMMAND [ARGS...] [--help]`. Commands are registered via decorators, with namespaces inferred from function names (e.g., `dev__env__start` → `dev env start`). The tool uses subprocess and execve for execution, focusing on environment management without direct server testing. Below, commands are grouped by namespace, with implementation notes for LLM parsing.

## Dev Namespace (Development Environment Management)
Manages the dev environment via overmind (process manager), ensuring idempotent operations and log handling.

- `dev env start [--no-daemon]`  
  Starts the dev environment using overmind and a Procfile. Checks for running processes, cleans up sockets, and logs to mcpzoo-overmind.log. Default: background mode; `--no-daemon` for foreground. No servers started.

- `dev env stop`  
  Terminates overmind to stop the dev environment. Simple subprocess call.

- `dev env restart`  
  Restarts via overmind restart. Assumes running state.

- `dev env status`  
  Checks overmind status; outputs process info or suggests starting.

- `dev env logs [--follow]`  
  Views logs from mcpzoo-overmind.log. Tails by default; `--follow` streams via overmind.

## Backend Namespace
Implements shell command execution inside Docker containers.

- `dev backend exec [BASH_COMMAND]`  
  Runs arbitrary commands in the backend container (`mcpzoo-dev`) using `docker exec -it`.

## Frontend Namespace
Handles local builds and dev servers (use dev servers only if explicitly requested).

- `dev frontend build [ARGS...]`  
  Builds frontend with `npm run build` in frontend dir, passing args.

- `dev frontend dev [ARGS...]`  
  Starts dev server with `npm run dev`. Avoid for testing per rules.

## Docker Namespace
Builds images, with production including full artifact prep.

- `dev docker build [ARGS...]`  
  Builds dev image (`mcpzoo-dev`) from `Dockerfile.development`.

- `prod docker build [ARGS...]`  
  Builds prod image (`mcpzoo`) after frontend build and backend sync. Includes run instructions.

